# Shrek OS — ADR-007 S2c: SEALED private trust base for the desktop-egress DoT re-pin client.
#
# This is NOT the host CA store and NOT a public webpki bundle. It is a curated, sealed set of exactly
# the TWO roots that anchor the sealed DoT resolvers' certificates, baked into dm-verity /usr. The
# supervisor's DoT client (egressd::dot) builds its rustls RootCertStore from ONLY this file — it never
# reads /etc/ssl, ca-certificates, or any uid-1000/NM-writable trust state. Combined with a sealed
# resolver IP set and an EXACT expected TLS hostname per resolver (egressd::dot::RESOLVERS), a
# compromised uid 1000 cannot steer the re-pin: it holds no authority over these roots, those IPs, or
# the hostname the cert must match. Fail-closed: no valid chain to one of these roots ⇒ no resolution
# ⇒ no pin (the baked deny skeleton stands).
#
# Roots (verified 2026-09-04: each live DoT endpoint's chain validates against ONLY these two):
#   1. SSL.com Root Certification Authority ECC   — anchors cloudflare-dns.com (1.1.1.1, 1.0.0.1:853)
#        SHA256 34:17:BB:06:CC:60:07:DA:1B:96:1C:92:0B:8A:B4:CE:3F:AD:82:0E:4A:A3:0B:9A:CB:C4:A7:4E:BD:CE:BC:65
#   2. DigiCert Global Root G3                    — anchors dns.quad9.net    (9.9.9.9, 149.112.112.112:853)
#        SHA256 31:AD:66:48:F8:10:41:38:C7:38:F3:9E:A4:32:01:33:39:3E:3A:18:CC:02:29:6E:F9:7C:2A:C9:EF:67:31:D0
# Provenance: distro ca-certificates store, cross-checked by fingerprint against the roots the live
# chains present/validate to. To rotate: replace a root here, re-verify the endpoint validates, re-seal.
